    "body": "## Summary\n\nFinal commit of ADR-054. Marks the ADR as Implemented with a **fixture-verified delta** — first cycle under the new \"synthetic-fixture verified\" category.\n\n## The verified delta\n\nPermanent fixture at `docs/adr054-rotate-test.html`. Screenshot at 2026-11-01 confirmed:\n\n```\nControl (no transform):     upright orange square\nrotate(45deg):              orange DIAMOND, corners at\n                            rotated positions\nrotate(30deg) rectangle:    tilted blue rectangle\n```\n\nAll three render correctly. The diamond is unmistakable; the tilted rectangle confirms non-45° angles work.\n\n**Diagnostic logs during verification** confirmed every layer:\n\n```\nADR-054-LAYOUT-INPUT: transform=rotate(45deg)   ← parse\nADR-054-LAYOUT: angle=45.00                     ← extraction\nADR-054-PAINT: angle=45.00 cx=72.00 cy=280.00   ← paint fires\n```\n\n## Two findings from fixture setup\n\n### 1. Shorthand `background:` / `border:` don't parse\n\nThe fixture's first version used:\n```css\nbackground: #d35400;\nborder: 2px solid #333;\n```\n**Both silently produced no visible fill.** Only the longhand forms render. The fixture was rewritten with:\n```css\nbackground-color: #d35400;\nborder-width: 2px; border-style: solid; border-color: #333;\n```\n\n**Pre-existing parser gap**, not ADR-054. Recorded in ADR-053's Post-ADR-054 note as a future ADR.\n\n### 2. `file://` URL accepts but fails at fetch\n\n`is_valid_url` whitelists `file://` (src/base/url.cpp:23-24), but `net/client.cpp` doesn't implement the scheme — returns status 0. The fixture test ran via `python3 -m http.server 8000` local serve.\n\n**Latent inconsistency.** Either add `file://` to the net layer or remove it from the validator. Separate ADR.\n\n## Honest delta framing\n\n**Synthetic fixture: visible.** Three boxes with correct rotation.\n**Wikipedia: zero PNG delta.** The magnifier's `translateY(-50%)` is parsed but not rotated (rotate parser skips it) — before/after screenshots on the HTML article are identical. Primary safety property confirmed.\n\n## The category matrix now has eight entries\n\n| Category | ADRs |\n|---|---|\n| PNG-verified (first viewport) | 040 / 042 / 043 |\n| Scroll-PNG (mid-scroll) | 045 / 051 pending |\n| Behaviorally-complete, visually-subtle | 044 |\n| Behaviorally-complete, visually-zero | 047 / 048 |\n| Measured, no target, deferred | 049 |\n| Layout-tree verified | 050 / 051 |\n| Log-verified | 052 |\n| **Synthetic-fixture verified** | **054 (this PR)** |\n\n## What this PR carries\n\n- ADR-054 → Implemented (four-layer implementation + fixture)\n- Post-ADR-054 note in ADR-053 (category matrix now eight entries; two findings recorded)\n- README row + CHANGELOG entry\n\n## Test count\n\n- 651 cases / 2490 assertions all pass\n- Documentation only; no code changes\n\nRefs #243\n",
